   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.2. Strengthened capacity of enterprises and their support systems to enhance productivity and sustainability</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vanuatu Institute of Technology has institutionalised the SYB programmes as one of their key entrepreneurship programmes. This initiative has empowered Vanuatu Institute of Technology with the necessary knowledge and skills to start and manage their own business development programmes within the institution.

This institution has now the capacity and access to practical tools and techniques to pursue entrepreneurship opportunities, create employment, and contribute to the economic development of Vanuatu.

This support has facilitated the delivery of relevant and market-driven skills development initiatives, ensuring that VIT&apos;s constituents are equipped with the skills demanded by the labour market. The International Labour Organization (ILO) has played a crucial role in supporting the Vanuatu Institute of Technology (VIT) in achieving its desired outcomes. Through various knowledge products and initiatives, the ILO has actively contributed to the development of VIT&apos;s capacity, ultimately strengthening its ability to meet the needs of its constituents. Through the provision of SYB TOT training and materials, technical capacity development, and the creation of knowledge products, the ILO has played a vital role in strengthening VIT&apos;s capacity to meet the needs of its constituents for enterprise sustainability.</narrative>
   </description>
